OpenBMC evb-ast2600: let mctpd auto-discover the endpoint (drop manual route, retry SetupEndpoint)

Rev-2 (PLDM Type 2) BMC-side delta on top of patch 0004. With the Zephyr node
now answering baseline MCTP control commands (MR2 control responder), mctpd's
SetupEndpoint enumerates the endpoint itself: it runs Get Endpoint ID, adopts
EID 18, adds the kernel route and neighbour, queries Get Message Type Support,
and publishes the endpoint on D-Bus so pldmd's platform-mc discovers and polls
it. Two changes to mctp-local.service:

  * Remove the manual "mctp route add 18 via mctpserial0" line. mctpd installs
    the route on successful SetupEndpoint, so the line is redundant; it is also
    the exact AF_MCTP netlink route/addr dump path that busy-loops on this
    kernel image (see docs/pldm-mctp-i3c-design.md sec 10b/10c).
  * Wrap the SetupEndpoint busctl call in a bounded retry loop (40 x 3 s). The
    endpoint is a separate Zephyr QEMU instance that may boot after the BMC, so
    the BusOwner call must be retried until the node answers.

Note (environment): on this image mctpd's own startup netlink dump
(fill_linkmap -> RTM_GETLINK|NLM_F_DUMP) busy-loops on the 6.6.92 AF_MCTP
kernel, so fully-automatic discovery cannot complete here; the MR1+MR2 Zephyr
responders were validated over the real kernel AF_MCTP transport by installing
the route with a raw-netlink helper and addressing EID 18 directly with
pldmtool (base GetTID/GetPLDMTypes + platform GetPDR/GetSensorReading all
answered correctly). See docs sec 10c for the full evidence.

---

### meta-evb/.../recipes-phosphor/mctp/files/mctp-local.service (modified)
diff --git a/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/files/mctp-local.service b/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/files/mctp-local.service
index 533df4c..bbac59e 100644
--- a/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/files/mctp-local.service
+++ b/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/files/mctp-local.service
@@ -11,8 +11,13 @@ ExecStart=mctp link serial /dev/ttyS0
 ExecStartPost=sleep 3
 ExecStartPost=mctp link set mctpserial0 up
 ExecStartPost=mctp addr add 8 dev mctpserial0
-ExecStartPost=mctp route add 18 via mctpserial0
-ExecStartPost=busctl call au.com.codeconstruct.MCTP1 /au/com/codeconstruct/mctp1/interfaces/mctpserial0 au.com.codeconstruct.MCTP.BusOwner1 SetupEndpoint ay 0
+# SetupEndpoint enumerates the remote endpoint (Get Endpoint ID over physical
+# addressing): mctpd then assigns/accepts its EID, adds the kernel route and
+# neighbour itself, queries Get Message Type Support, and publishes it on D-Bus
+# so pldmd's platform-mc discovers it. No manual "mctp route add" is needed
+# (and the CLI route/addr dump paths busy-loop on this image). The endpoint
+# (a Zephyr QEMU instance) may boot after the BMC, so retry until it answers.
+ExecStartPost=/bin/sh -c 'n=0; while [ $n -lt 40 ]; do busctl call au.com.codeconstruct.MCTP1 /au/com/codeconstruct/mctp1/interfaces/mctpserial0 au.com.codeconstruct.MCTP.BusOwner1 SetupEndpoint ay 0 && exit 0; n=$((n+1)); sleep 3; done; exit 1'
 
 [Install]
 WantedBy=mctpd.service

